        "reinforce": [
          "Walk both rooms in prep before you place a single panel. You are on the top floor, so nothing is coming down on you — every threat comes from below you or from outside the building. Reinforce in that order of threat, not in the order the walls light up.",
          "First: any floor hatch inside 2F Trophy Room or 2F Statuary Room. Attackers below can climb up through an open hatch and land behind whoever is watching the outside wall. If a hatch exists in either room it is the single most expensive thing you can leave open. Check for one yourself — do not assume from another site.",
          "Second: the site wall with open air behind it. That is the one a hard breacher can hit from the outside surface without ever putting a body in the building, which means your randoms never even get a chance to punish it. you places this one himself so he knows exactly which panel his claw has to cover.",
          "Third: if the two rooms are separated by a wall rather than an open doorway, leave that wall SOFT. You are two players holding a two-room site — you need to shoot through that seam and rotate through it. Reinforcing it turns the site into two one-room fights you will lose separately.",
          "Nothing else in the site gets a panel from you two. If a random wants to reinforce further out, fine, but you are not spending your reinforcements on cosmetic walls while the outside wall is still bare."
        ],
        "job": [
          "Prep: reinforce the outside-facing wall, then throw one Electroclaw so it covers that panel — put the claw on the floor a step back from the wall or on the surface beside it, not centred on the panel itself. A claw stuck out in the open dies to the first Twitch drone that pokes a window; a claw set back forces the drone to come into the room where your duo can hear it and you can shoot it.",
          "Hold your remaining claw. Do not dump both in prep. If they EMP the wall you want a replacement in hand, and a Thatcher carries three EMPs so you will get hit more than once. When the first EMP lands, wait for the throw animation of the breach charge rather than re-clawing instantly into a second EMP.",
          "Round start: anchor in the room with the outside wall, deep, off the wall, angled so a new hole opens into your crosshair instead of onto your body. Do not stand where you would have to turn to see it.",
          "Call the spawn out loud the second you know it — Fountain, Main Road or Ruins. That single call is worth more to your randoms than anything you do with a gun.",
          "When the breach goes up and the hole opens, take one shot at whatever comes through and then reassess. If you cannot win that hole cleanly, leave it — see fallback. You are the utility player here, not the entry fragger; trading yourself out on the first hole gives them a free two-room site."
        ],
        "duoJob": [
          "One job: anchor in the other site room facing the doorway that connects the two rooms, and stay there. You do not roam, you do not push the hole, you do not chase a runner.",
          "One trigger: the moment a wall or the floor opens anywhere in the site, throw one Kiba Barrier across that hole, then go straight back to your angle. Aim at the surface just under the hole so the barrier grows up into it. The Kiba is bulletproof — they cannot shoot it out, including with Buck's Skeleton Key — so every second they spend on it is a second they are stuck in a doorway you and you already have covered.",
          "Take the laser off your gun if you run one. You are going to be holding an ADS angle on a doorway for long stretches, and the laser is visible to the enemy the whole time you are aiming. It tells them exactly where your head is before they even peek.",
          "Keep your barriers for holes, not for pre-round walling. Sealing a doorway in prep just tells them where you are and where you are not.",
          "If you get a headshot and the room goes quiet, do not step out to confirm the kill. Reload, reset on the same angle, wait for the second body."
        ],
        "anchor": "you in the site room containing the reinforced outside wall — deep in the room, off the wall, angled onto it. your duo in the other site room, facing the connecting doorway, behind hard cover, with the soft seam on his flank so he can shoot through it if you calls a body. That puts two guns on anything that enters either room, from two different directions, without either of you having to move.",
        "fallback": "Trigger to fall back is simple: the outside wall is down and you did not get the first body. Do not trade in the open. you backs off through the seam into your duo's room and both of you hold that connecting doorway, so they have to come in one at a time through a gap your duo can Kiba. Give up the room, keep the crossfire. If the bomb is already down and you are both alive with one random, do not push out to the hole — hold the doorway and make them come to the defuser. Pick substitutes if these are taken: you goes Mute and puts a GC90 on the same outside wall (he carries four, so one on the wall and one deeper as a backup); your duo goes Melusi and puts the Banshee facing the doorway with its armoured front toward the attackers, because it is only bulletproof from the front.",
